                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Good and bad, but mostly good.\n\nThe Bad: There's a minor issue at the moment with unintentional Artificial Locomotion causing VR Sickness in extreme cases (like me). There are no fixed points of reference in the distance and the fireflies wafting in one direction can accidentally cause a problem in people especially sensitive to VR sickness. \n\nThe Good: The game is simple, but engaging. If you're a fan of puzzle games, the ability to play with an interactive sliding puzzle in VR is an amazing experience. The game could use more levels, but the levels that are in already are a ton of fun to play and mull over for several hours. I especially like that Solaright takes full advantage of the VR universe to make the puzzle not only three dimensional, but also colorful and interesting. \n\nThe puzzle itself could use some variation in appearance from level to level, and the game could use a little bit of story, but all in all, a ton of fun at a good price.",
